codex
The first proof attempt exposed a backend limitation: this K version rejects claims whose entire left side is a function term. I’m adapting the semantics to an operational call machine with explicit environments and call frames. That keeps the claims as configuration reachability claims and, importantly, lets `kprove` use circularity exactly at recursive `factorize_from` invocations.
apply patch
