The constructor-based route is now executing in the prover, but simplification deliberately stops after a short same-symbol chain. I’m converting the machine transition constructor into a partial K function and placing it under a non-functional proof wrapper. That gives concrete execution full normalization while keeping the reachability claim itself non-functional—the exact boundary this backend supports.
